 of rejecting the invalid range with an explanation that the start date is later than the end date.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-23\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing category not identified to user\", \"actual\": \"Submitting the Add Transaction form without selecting a Category (still showing 'Select category' placeholder) silently failed to create the transaction, but no error text or visual indicator identified the category as missing.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-24\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Deleting a category assigned to existing transactions is not blocked and does not require reassignment\", \"actual\": \"Deleted \\\"Office Supplies\\\" expense category which had 2 assigned transactions (\\\"Office Supplies - Printer Paper & Ink\\\" $-156.00 and \\\"Office Equipment\\\" $-890.00). Confirmation dialog only warned \\\"Transactions using this category will not be deleted\\\" with a plain Cancel/Delete choice - no reassignment option or blocking. After confirming, the category was permanently removed (Expense Categories 8→7) and the 2 transactions were left orphaned with a blank/empty Category cell in the Transactions table (previously showed \\\"Office Supplies\\\"). This violates the requirement that deletion of an in-use category should be blocked or require reassignment - instead it silently leaves transactions with no category.\", \"evidence\": \"Transactions table rows for \\\"Office Supplies - Printer Paper & Ink\\\" and \\\"Office Equipment\\\" now show empty Category cell (previously \\\"Office Supplies\\\") after category deletion.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After adding an Aug 24, 2026 expense of $125.50, Dashboard immediately reflected Monthly Expenses $126, Net Profit/Loss -$126, and the new transaction appeared at top of Recent Transactions without page reload.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Toggling Tax Related ON on a test expense (Rent, $200, Aug 24 2026) updated Tax Summary 2026: Total Deductible Expenses $0→$200, Net Taxable Income $0→-$200, Deductible Expenses by Category showed Rent 100%, All Tax-Related Transactions 0→1. Toggling it back OFF and saving reverted all figures exactly to $0.00 / empty states / 0 transactions, confirming bidirectional real-time sync between transaction tax-related status and annual tax summary.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Added new expense transaction \\\"IX18 QA Rent Test\\\" $200.00 with category Rent. Categories page immediately reflected the change: Rent category transaction count went from 2 transactions/$4,400 total to 3 transactions/$4,600 total, without any manual refresh. Additionally, when the \\\"Office Supplies\\\" category was deleted earlier, its category card was immediately removed from the list (Expense Categories 8→7). Deleting/editing transactions elsewhere in this session (e.g., FT9 test transaction) also correctly incremented/decremented the relevant category's count and total in real time.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicked \\\"Print Report\\\" button on Tax Summary page for year 2024 (populated with 18 tax-related transactions and full category breakdowns). No application error occurred - console message count remained unchanged (1 pre-existing unrelated React \\\"key prop\\\" warning, no new errors), page did not crash, and UI remained fully rendered and interactive after the click (browser's native print dialog invocation is expected and not capturable/blocking in this automated context, but no JS exception or broken state resulted).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Transactions table displays Date, Description, Category, Reference (or — if none), Amount (with +/- sign), and Tax (✓ mark) columns for every row, plus a footer showing Total Income and Total Expenses for the currently filtered result set.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After adding the $125.50 Aug 2026 expense, Monthly Expenses updated to $126 and Net Profit/Loss to -$126, consistent with $0 income - $126 expenses; new transaction appeared correctly in Recent Transactions.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Chart axis labels lack precision for small non-zero values\", \"actual\": \"After adding a $125.50 expense (the only current-month transaction), the 'Income vs Expenses' dashboard chart's Y-axis shows all five tick labels as '$0k', making the non-zero $126 monthly expense indistinguishable from zero on the axis.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
